    "content": "\n## Request boundary\n\nFiles under an `api/` directory of the routes dir are API routes; they are served by the same generated entry as pages and are never prerendered. Requests and responses are the Web `Request` and `Response` objects.\n\n## Handler shape\n\nAn API route default-exports either a Hono app (mounted with `app.route()`) or a function `(ctx) => Response` receiving `{ request, params, env, platform }` (mounted with `app.all()`). Keep input parsing, validation, and response serialization visible in the route.\n\n### app/routes/api/hello.ts\n\n```ts\n// Files under an api/ directory are API routes. Default-export a Hono\n// app (mounted with app.route()) or a function (ctx) => Response\n// (mounted with app.all()).\nexport default function hello(ctx: {\n  request: Request;\n  params: Record<string, string>;\n  env: Record<string, string | undefined>;\n  platform?: unknown;\n}) {\n  const url = new URL(ctx.request.url);\n  return Response.json({ hello: url.searchParams.get('name') ?? 'world' });\n}\n```\n\nThe same default-export contract applies at every depth: `app/routes/api/items/[id].ts` serves `/api/items/:id` with `params` populated from the path.\n\n## Runtime fit\n\nUse Deno-first tasks and avoid Node-only assumptions in docs examples.\n",
    "html": "<h2>Request boundary</h2>\n<p>Files under an <code>api/</code> directory of the routes dir are API routes; they are served by the same generated entry as pages and are never prerendered. Requests and responses are the Web <code>Request</code> and <code>Response</code> objects.</p>\n<h2>Handler shape</h2>\n<p>An API route default-exports either a Hono app (mounted with <code>app.route()</code>) or a function <code>(ctx) =&gt; Response</code> receiving <code>{ request, params, env, platform }</code> (mounted with <code>app.all()</code>). Keep input parsing, validation, and response serialization visible in the route.</p>\n<h3>app/routes/api/hello.ts</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-ts\">// Files under an api/ directory are API routes. Default-export a Hono\n// app (mounted with app.route()) or a function (ctx) =&gt; Response\n// (mounted with app.all()).\nexport default function hello(ctx: {\n  request: Request;\n  params: Record&lt;string, string&gt;;\n  env: Record&lt;string, string | undefined&gt;;\n  platform?: unknown;\n}) {\n  const url = new URL(ctx.request.url);\n  return Response.json({ hello: url.searchParams.get(&#39;name&#39;) ?? &#39;world&#39; });\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>The same default-export contract applies at every depth: <code>app/routes/api/items/[id].ts</code> serves <code>/api/items/:id</code> with <code>params</code> populated from the path.</p>\n<h2>Runtime fit</h2>\n<p>Use Deno-first tasks and avoid Node-only assumptions in docs examples.</p>\n"
